Now enemies.js.

Define ENEMY_TYPES with hp, speed, damage, accuracy, fireInterval, color scheme, scale, score, name. Types: soldier, scout, heavy, sniper, elite, boss.

Enemy class:

```js
export class Enemy {
 constructor(scene, type, pos, level, rng) {
   this.type = type; ...
   this.group = new THREE.Group();
   this.mats = [];
   build body
   position
   this.hp/maxHp scaling: base * (1 + (level.n-1)*0.12), boss multiply.
   this.hitMeshes = [];
   this.muzzle = object
   this.fireTimer = 1 + rng*1.5
   this.losTimer = 0; this.hasLos = false
   this.phase = rng*6.28
   this.strafe = rng > .5 ? 1 : -1
   this.flashTimer = 0
   this.dead=false; this.deathT=0
   this.group.position
   this.radius=0.5*scale
 }
 takeDamage(amount, part, ctx) {...}
 update(dt, ctx) {...}
 die()...
 resetFlash
}
```

Materials per instance to allow flash: helper create mat returns MeshStandardMaterial and push to this.mats with base emissive? Use `emissive` black; on hit set emissive 0xff3322 intensity 1, decay.

Body build:
- legs: hip at y=0.9; two box legs 0.19 x 0.78 x 0.2 at x ±0.16, y 0.45. Pivot rotation at top: to swing legs naturally, create pivot group at y 0.9 with mesh offset y -0.39. Use pivot.
- torso: box 0.56 x 0.62 x 0.32 at y 1.22; vest overlay 0.5x0.4x0.34 at y 1.24 darker; pouches.
- shoulders: spheres/boxes at ±0.33, y 1.45.
- arms: pivot groups at shoulder y1.45, arm mesh offset y-0.22, rotate toward front holding gun (rotation.x ≈ -1.1); gun in hands at (0, 1.32, -0.35)? Simplify: arms angled forward and a gun mesh at y 1.25, z -0.34.
- head: sphere or box at y 1.72; helmet; visor emissive for night/elite.
- backpack.
- drop shadow: circle sprite? Real shadows from sun. castShadow true on parts.

Scale group per type: soldier 1, scout .93, heavy 1.16, sniper 1.02, elite 1.1, boss 1.5.

Hit meshes: torso, head, pelvis, legs. Mark userData.enemy = this, part.

Colors per type:
soldier: uniform 0x6f6b4f (khaki), helmet 0x4e4b38, vest 0x33352c, visor 0x88ffcc faint, accent.
scout: 0x3c4a42, dark, red visor.
heavy: 0x4a4f44, bulky, heavy helmet.
sniper: 0x5a5f57, ghillie? hood.
elite: 0x3a2f33 with red visor and emissive.
boss: 0x2a1c1c, red emissive, larger, spikes? Add shoulder plates.

Enemy update details:
```js
update(dt, ctx) {
 if (this.dead) { death animation; return; }
 const p = ctx.playerPos;
 const dx = p.x - this.group.position.x, dz = p.z - this.group.position.z;
 const dist = Math.hypot(dx,dz);
 ...
 // LOS check every 0.18s
 if (losTimer<=0 && dist < 50) { this.hasLos = ctx.checkLOS(this.group.position, p); losTimer=0.18; }
 // facing player
 targetRot = Math.atan2(dx, dz) (model forward is +Z? body gun at -Z, so forward is -Z. To face player, rotation.y = atan2(dx,dz)+PI? Let's define model faces -Z. A rotation.y = 0 makes forward -Z. We want forward direction toward player: direction vector (dx,dz); angle = atan2(-dx, -dz)? For object rotated by y, forward -Z maps to (-sin(y), -cos(y)). To equal normalized (dx,dz): -sin(y)=dx/d, -cos(y)=dz/d → y = atan2(-dx, -dz). Use that.
 // movement
 let moveX=0, moveZ=0;
 preferred range from type: soldier 14, scout 6, heavy 12, sniper 32, elite 10, boss 8.
 if (!hasLos || dist > preferred*1.35) toward player
 else if dist < preferred*0.65 → away
 else strafe: perpendicular * strafeDir, switch direction with timer.
 // speed
 const spd = type.speed * (hasLos ? 1 : 0.85);
 move...
 // resolve collisions via ctx.resolveCircle(vec2)
 // separation
 // bounds
 // clamp inside ctx.bounds
 // animate walk: legs swing based on movement magnitude & time
 // shooting
 if (hasLos && dist < type.range && fireTimer <=0 && !ctx.playerDead) shoot(ctx, dist)
}
```

Important enemy doesn't jitter at obstacle. Use `ctx.resolveCircle(x,z,r)` returning new [x,z]. Call after computing candidate. Add wall avoid: if no LOS and blocked, strafing; simple approach: if movement blocked heavily, pick strafe direction. We can detect pos change < expected*0.3 and set strafe dir flip.

Simplify collision: try move; call resolve; if moved less than 30% of desired, set this.blockedTime += dt, and apply perpendicular when blocked. Fine.

LOS: use ctx.occluders via Raycaster; origin enemy chest (y=1.5*scale), target player eye. Implement in main with raycaster reused. Each enemy call uses a global raycaster from main; ctx.checkLOS(originVec, targetVec) returns bool. In main function:

```js
const losRay = new THREE.Raycaster();
function checkLOS(from, to) {
 const dir = to.clone().sub(from); const dist = dir.length(); dir.normalize();
 losRay.set(from, dir); losRay.far = dist - 0.3;
 const hits = losRay.intersectObjects(world.occluders, false);
 return hits.length === 0 || hits[0].distance > dist - 0.5;
}
